menu "MicroTech connectivity manager"

config CONNECTIVITY_MANAGER_TASK_STACK
    int "Connectivity policy worker stack depth"
    default 6144
    range 4096 8192

config CONNECTIVITY_MANAGER_QUEUE_DEPTH
    int "Connectivity policy command queue depth"
    default 8
    range 4 32

config CONNECTIVITY_MANAGER_MAX_PROFILES
    int "Saved Wi-Fi networks retained at the same time"
    default 4
    range 1 5
    help
        The upper bound of 5 keeps the password-free profile snapshot inside
        the event-bus UI payload budget. The persisted record always reserves
        five entry slots, so a record written by a build with more slots stays
        readable after this value is lowered: loading keeps the first
        CONNECTIVITY_MANAGER_MAX_PROFILES entries, clamps the selected index
        into that range, and rewrites the record. Entries beyond the limit are
        dropped by that rewrite. A structurally invalid record is still
        rejected rather than partially loaded.

endmenu
